<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ikšķile</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Üxküll</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ikšķile, German Üxküll, is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-dvina">Daugava</a> river in Latvia, south-east of Riga. There the missionary Meinhard built a church and one of the first stone castles in the Baltic region in the 1180s. It was the first seat of the bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a> before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> moved to Riga in 1201.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ikskile.jpg" alt="Ikšķile" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Latvia United at Latvian Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ik%C5%A1%C4%B7iles_bazn%C4%ABcas_drupas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
